# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in real values. Never commit `.env.local`.

# Where the browser sends API requests.
#
# Deployed, this is the relative path `/api`, which `next.config.ts` proxies to
# the API. That keeps the auth cookie first-party — served from a different
# origin it would be a third-party cookie, and browsers that block those
# (Chrome incognito by default) discard it, so signing in silently fails.
#
# Locally both apps are on `localhost`, which is already the same site, so
# pointing straight at the API is simpler and one hop shorter.
#
# Local:      http://localhost:3001
# Production: /api
#
# This is a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable: it is inlined into the browser bundle at
# build time, so changing it on Vercel requires a redeploy, not just a restart.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Only needed when NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is `/api`. Server-side: the browser never
# sees it. Absent, no proxy is set up and the app calls NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL
# directly.
#
# Production: https://<your-service>.up.railway.app
# API_ORIGIN=
